<newsitem itemid="71486" id="root" date="1996-09-23" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Crown Products turnover on the rise.</title>
<headline>Crown Products turnover on the rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		0.4 earnings	 vs 2.3 loss</p>
<p> Pretax		     0.10 profit	  vs 0.28 loss</p>
<p> Turnover		   16.60		  vs 2.95</p>
<p> Operating result	 0.47 profit	  vs 0.20 loss</p>
<p> Interest		   0.37		   vs 0.08</p>
<p> Tax			  nil		    vs 0.003</p>
<p>NOTE - Comparisons are with the 18 months ending June 30, 1995 as the company has changed its year-end to December 31.  </p>
<p>There was no dividend. Crown said shareholder approval for reduction of the share premium account at the October 19 extraordianry general meeting &quot;will enable Crown to pay dividends out of future profits.&quot;</p>
<p>Chairman Michael Hughes said turnover in the second six months of 1996 is expected to continue to grow but the full benefit of acquisitions and rationalisation will not be seen until next year. The company said it also intends to seek admission to the official list of the stock exchange &quot;at an early date.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
